# Applies to `moon publish` / `moon package` only -- the build is unaffected,
# so CI still compiles everything from the repo.
#
# Patterns resolve against the WORKSPACE root, not this module. A directory
# pattern naming a sibling (e.g. "modules/") therefore empties that module's
# archive, silently. Keep this file to whole test-harness directories.
#
# `*_test.mbt` / `*_wbtest.mbt` are deliberately NOT excluded. `moon.pkg` ships
# verbatim, `import { .. } for "test"` blocks included, so stripping the test
# files leaves those imports with nothing that uses them and every archive
# reports `unused_package` -- 34 warnings across 27 packages when we did strip
# them, two of those a module importing itself. `moonbitlang/core` ships its
# tests for the same reason.

# Test-harness packages, driven from outside `moon test` (deno task / bun test)
# and not buildable by a consumer. Excluded as whole directories, so each
# `moon.pkg` goes with its sources and no import is left dangling.
_tests/
bun_test/
_interop_test/
